<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-SFE wheat futures edge down again.</title>
<headline>RTRS-SFE wheat futures edge down again.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-03-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sydney Futures Exchange (SFE) wheat unexpectedly came back in low-level trading on Monday.</p>
<p>Only three lots traded, in July 1997, which fell by 50 cents to A$182.00 a tonne.</p>
<p>&quot;It's very slow. There's not much more you can say about it,&quot; one broker said.</p>
<p>An ask quote of A$182.00 the nearby March 1997 contract was lower than anticipated and did not reflect tightness in the physical market, he said.</p>
<p>Futures settlement prices came back by A$2.00-A$3.00 across the range of contracts.  </p>
